"""Tower Breadcrumbs development pages; maintain claims against the Android source."""
def build(page):
    page('/tower-breadcrumbs/', 'Tower Breadcrumbs — Offline GPS & Reception Trails for Android',
         'Record GPS breadcrumbs, save observed cellular reception and find a bearing back to a recorded point. Tower Breadcrumbs for Android is coming soon.',
         """
<style>
.tb{--ink:#252c28;--paper:#faf7ee;--rust:#993e22;color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);padding:clamp(20px,5vw,64px);margin:24px 0;border:1px solid #8b9284}
.tb h1,.tb h2,.tb h3,.tb p,.tb a,.tb li{color:var(--ink)}
.tb h1{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(36px,6vw,64px);line-height:1.08;max-width:12ch;margin:18px 0 24px}
.tb h2{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:30px;margin:32px 0 16px}
.tb p,.tb li{font-size:17px;line-height:1.65;max-width:65ch}
.tb .kicker{font:700 12px/1.5 monospace;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:var(--rust)}
.tb .hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 180px;gap:36px;align-items:center}
.tb h1::first-line{color:var(--ink)}
.tb .hero img{height:auto;width:180px;max-width:100%;border:1px solid #8b9284}
.tb .facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border-top:2px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid #8b9284;margin:32px 0}
.tb .facts p{padding:16px 16px 16px 0;margin:0;font:700 13px/1.6 monospace}
.tb a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px}
.tb .shots{display:flex;gap:20px;overflow:auto;padding-bottom:16px}
.tb .shots img{height:auto;width:240px;max-width:70vw;border:1px solid #8b9284}
@media(max-width:600px){.tb .hero{grid-template-columns:1fr}.tb .hero img{width:100px;grid-row:1}.tb .facts{grid-template-columns:1fr}.tb .facts p{padding:10px 0}.tb{margin:12px 0}}
</style>
<article class="tb">
<div class="hero"><div><p class="kicker">TOWER BREADCRUMBS / ANDROID</p><h1>Leave a trail.<br>Find your way back.</h1><p>Keep a record of where your phone had reception. When it disappears, use GPS to see the direction and straight-line distance back to a saved point.</p><p><strong>Coming soon.</strong> A development preview is being tested. There is no public Google Play download yet.</p></div><img src="/assets/apps/tower-breadcrumbs/icon.png" width="512" height="512" alt="Tower Breadcrumbs compass and trail icon"></div>
<div class="facts"><p>GPS BREADCRUMBS<br>Saved on your phone</p><p>OFFLINE MAP IMPORTS<br>Prepare before departure</p><p>ONE-TIME AD REMOVAL<br>Planned US price: $0.99</p></div>
<h2>Back to a place you actually recorded.</h2><p>“Last reception” saves where your phone reported cellular service. “Last data” separately records where Android validated a cellular internet connection. Select either point to see a true-north bearing and distance from your current GPS position.</p>
<h2>Read the landscape. Keep the details close.</h2><p>A north-up map, clear coordinates and a compact return panel keep the important information together. The logbook holds your journeys and lets you export a selected trail as CSV.</p>
<div class="shots"><a href="/assets/apps/tower-breadcrumbs/development-map.png"><img src="/assets/apps/tower-breadcrumbs/development-map.png" alt="Tower Breadcrumbs development screen with a simulated GPS trail, high-contrast return controls and offline coordinate grid" width="1080" height="2400" loading="lazy"></a></div><p>Development build shown with a simulated trail. The background is a coordinate grid, not a downloaded road map.</p><h2>Bring your maps and cell data.</h2><p>Import a regional raster MBTiles map before you leave. The coordinate grid and saved trail work without internet; roads appear where your imported map has tiles. This first version has no built-in area downloader or worldwide tower database.</p><p>Import estimated cell locations from a compatible CSV. Carrier names such as T-Mobile or Verizon and radio labels such as 5G/NR, 4G/LTE and 3G appear when supplied by the dataset. Unknown fields stay unknown. Imported positions may be estimated cell centers rather than physical towers.</p>
<h2>Designed for the field, with honest limits.</h2><p>GPS needs a usable satellite view. The bearing is a straight line, not a safe walking route. Terrain, carrier compatibility, outages and network changes can all affect reception. A saved point or nearby cell does not guarantee service. Keep an independent navigation and emergency plan.</p>
<p>The planned app is free with ads and a one-time $0.99 US purchase to remove all ads. Store availability and local pricing will be confirmed at launch. Full-screen ads are excluded from active GPS navigation.</p>
<p><a href="/tower-breadcrumbs/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> · <a href="/tower-breadcrumbs/support/">Support and preparation guide</a></p>
</article>
""", 'https://tripperdeelabs.com/assets/apps/tower-breadcrumbs/icon.png')
    page('/tower-breadcrumbs/privacy/', 'Tower Breadcrumbs Privacy Policy',
         'How Tower Breadcrumbs stores GPS trails, imports maps, handles advertising and verifies optional ad-removal purchases.',
         """
<section><h1>Tower Breadcrumbs privacy policy</h1><p>Effective November 5, 2026. Developer: TripperDeeLabs. Package: <code>com.tripperdeelabs.towerbreadcrumbs</code>. This policy describes the current Android development build and its configured SDKs.</p>
<h2>GPS and cellular observations</h2><p>When you start recording, Tower Breadcrumbs stores your phone’s precise latitude and longitude, time, accuracy, reported cellular service, Android-validated cellular connectivity, available signal strength, carrier name and cell identifiers. These records remain in the app’s private local database. The app does not upload your trail to TripperDeeLabs or operate a cloud account or trail-sync service.</p><p>Navigation without recording uses a live GPS position to calculate a bearing and distance but does not add trail points. GPS runs only after you start it, with an ongoing Android notification, and stops when you choose Stop. The app does not start recording automatically after reboot.</p>
<h2>Permissions</h2><p>Precise location enables GPS breadcrumbs and permitted cellular readings. Phone-state access reads network information; the app does not read your call log, contacts or call audio or place calls. Notification permission supports the visible GPS status. Internet access is used by Google advertising, consent and purchase services. File import/export uses Android’s document picker so you choose the files.</p>
<h2>Maps, cell files and exports</h2><p>Imported offline maps and estimated cell-location CSV files are copied into app-private storage. Their original files remain where you stored them. Exported CSV files can contain sensitive location history, time, carrier and cellular identifiers. You choose the destination and whether to share them. Exports remain separate from the app and must be deleted separately.</p>
<h2>Google advertising and consent</h2><p>The app includes Google Mobile Ads (AdMob) and Google’s User Messaging Platform. Google’s SDKs may collect and share IP addresses (including approximate location derived from them), advertising/device identifiers, app interactions and diagnostic information for advertising, measurement and fraud prevention. SDK network data is encrypted in transit. The app does not intentionally supply its stored precise coordinates or cellular journal to the advertising SDK.</p><p>Regional consent and privacy choices depend on the app’s published consent configuration. Where required, advertising privacy choices can be reopened in Settings. Current preview builds use Google’s sample ad units; live ads and regional messages are not yet configured for release.</p>
<h2>Purchases</h2><p>Google Play processes the optional one-time ad-removal purchase. The app receives purchase status, product identifiers and tokens to acknowledge purchases and restore access. It does not receive your payment-card details. Ad removal disables all banner and full-screen ads; it does not stop necessary Google Play purchase checks or erase information already processed by Google. Cached entitlement may persist until a later successful Play verification.</p>
<h2>Retention and deletion</h2><p>Recorded trails remain until you delete them in Logbook or remove app data. Imported map copies and cell estimates can be removed in Offline. Android cloud backup and device transfer are disabled for this app. Uninstalling or clearing storage can remove local records permanently. TripperDeeLabs cannot recover trails kept only on your device. Original imports and exported files are outside this deletion. Google’s policies govern data held by its services.</p>
<h2>Support and changes</h2><p>If you contact <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a>, we receive the email address, message and any attachments you choose to provide. We use them to handle your request and retain them as needed for that purpose. Avoid sending sensitive trails unless necessary. Contact the same address about privacy or correspondence deletion. We will update this page when data practices change.</p>
<p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a> · <a href="/privacy/">Website privacy</a> · <a href="/tower-breadcrumbs/">App overview</a> · <a href="/tower-breadcrumbs/support/">App support</a></p></section>
""")
    page('/tower-breadcrumbs/support/', 'Tower Breadcrumbs Support',
         'Prepare offline maps, record GPS breadcrumbs, read carrier labels and restore Tower Breadcrumbs ad removal.',
         """
<section><h1>Tower Breadcrumbs support</h1><p>The app is in development for Android 10 and later. Contact <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com?subject=Tower%20Breadcrumbs%20support">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a>.</p>
<h2>Before heading out</h2><ol><li>Import a legally obtained regional raster MBTiles map in Offline. PNG, JPEG and WebP tiles are supported, up to 500 MB. Vector PBF tiles are not supported.</li><li>Optionally import cell locations as CSV with latitude,longitude,id,carrier,radio,source headers. OpenCellID-style lat/lon files are also supported, up to 20,000 rows. Carrier names and radio types must come from the source; check its license and data age.</li><li>Go outdoors, choose Record a trail and allow precise location. Optional phone-state access supplies cellular details.</li><li>Check that coordinates and the point count update before you depend on the recorded trail.</li></ol>
<h2>Returning to reception</h2><p>Select Last reception or Last data on Map. The first is a recorded service indication; the second is an Android-validated cellular connection. The compass is north-up and displays a true bearing, not your phone’s magnetic heading. Distance is straight-line only. Check terrain yourself.</p>
<h2>Understanding tower labels</h2><p>Labels show the imported carrier and radio type. NR maps to 5G, LTE to 4G, UMTS/WCDMA/HSPA to 3G, and GSM/EDGE/GPRS to 2G. Numeric network codes remain PLMN codes unless the file provides a carrier name. An estimated cell location is not a surveyed tower or coverage guarantee.</p>
<h2>GPS or reception appears unavailable</h2><p>Check Android Location and precise-location permission. Move outdoors and give GPS time to acquire satellites. Stale or low-accuracy positions are not used for return bearings. Cell readings depend on your hardware, permissions, SIM and Android restrictions. A Wi-Fi connection is not recorded as cellular internet. Some 5G non-standalone connections may be reported as LTE by Android.</p>
<h2>Saving, exporting and stopping</h2><p>Use Stop GPS &amp; Save to finish recording. GPS navigation also has a Stop control and a notification action. Select a journey in Logbook to review it or export CSV. The map draws the most recent 2,000 points of the selected trail; the export contains all saved points. Avoid uninstalling or clearing storage during troubleshooting.</p>
<h2>Ad removal</h2><p>The planned one-time US price is $0.99. Actual prices come from Google Play after the product is configured. Use Restore purchases with the purchasing Google account. Preview installs may show Purchase unavailable; no charge can be made until the Play product and testing distribution are configured.</p>
<h2>Report a problem</h2><p>Include app version, phone model, Android version, whether a SIM was present, and the steps that caused the issue. You do not need to send exact coordinates or a complete trail.</p><p><a href="/tower-breadcrumbs/">App overview</a> · <a href="/tower-breadcrumbs/privacy/">Privacy policy</a></p></section>
""")
